target/
    .idea/
    *.iml
    test-output/
    ```


    In the terminal, run these three commands one after the other:
    `git add .`
    `git commit -m "Initial framework setup"`
    `git branch -M main`


    In the terminal, type this to create and switch to your development branch:
    `git checkout -b dev`


    Go to GitHub.com, create a **New Repository** (leave it completely empty, no README). Copy the repository URL, then run these final commands in your IntelliJ terminal (replace the URL with your actual GitHub URL):
    `git remote add origin [https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO_NAME.git](https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO_NAME.git)`
    `git push -u origin main`
    `git push -u origin dev`